AWS Auto Scaling – Important Interview Questions for DevOps Engineers
Auto Scaling is one of the most important services in AWS for building highly available and scalable applications. Here are some commonly asked Auto Scaling interview questions.
🔹 1. What is Auto Scaling in AWS?
 Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances based on traffic or demand to maintain performance and reduce cost.
🔹 2. What are the main components of Auto Scaling?
 • Launch Template / Launch Configuration
 • Auto Scaling Group (ASG)
 • Scaling Policies
🔹 3. What is Desired Capacity?
 Desired capacity is the number of EC2 instances that the Auto Scaling Group tries to maintain at all times.
🔹 4. What is the difference between Scale Out and Scale In?
 • Scale Out – Adding more EC2 instances when demand increases.
 • Scale In – Removing EC2 instances when demand decreases.
🔹 5. What is a Health Check in Auto Scaling?
 Auto Scaling monitors instance health using EC2 or Load Balancer health checks. If an instance becomes unhealthy, it automatically replaces it.
🔹 6. What are Scaling Policies?
 Scaling policies define when Auto Scaling should add or remove instances based on CloudWatch metrics.
💡 Common metrics used for scaling:
 • CPU Utilization
 • Network traffic
 • ALB request count
📌 Auto Scaling helps achieve:
 ✔ High availability
 ✔ Fault tolerance
 ✔ Cost optimization
